.\" nimbus-update(1) - manual page, shipped by nimbusos-release
.TH NIMBUS-UPDATE 1 "2026-11-17" "NimbusOS" "NimbusOS"
.SH NAME
nimbus-update \- check, install and configure NimbusOS updates
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nimbus-update
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nimbus-update
holds all update logic of a NimbusOS system. NimbusOS's own packages come
from the NimbusOS APT repository; Debian packages come from Debian's
mirrors. The Nimbus Control Center calls this tool through its privileged
helper; administrators can use it directly.
.PP
Debian security updates are installed daily by
.BR unattended-upgrades (8).
NimbusOS updates follow the policy set with
.BR "nimbus-update policy" .
The system never restarts on its own.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show the installed version, the channel, the policy, and the result of the
last check (pending updates, problems, whether a restart is required).
.TP
.BR check " [" \-\-scheduled ]
Refresh the package lists, explain any failure (name resolution, secure
connection, signature, expired metadata, unreachable server), list pending
updates grouped as Security, NimbusOS and Debian, fetch the signed release
notes, and store the result in
.IR /var/lib/nimbusos/update\-status.json .
A repository whose signature can't be verified is reported as an error,
never as "no updates".
With
.B \-\-scheduled
(used by the daily timer) nothing is done when the policy is
.BR off ,
or while another update run holds the lock (that run refreshes the status
itself), and the exit status is always 0.
.TP
.B install
Refresh the package lists and run a full upgrade, non-interactively,
keeping locally changed configuration files. Waits up to ten minutes for a
running apt or unattended-upgrades to finish.
.TP
.B auto
The
.B automatic
policy: upgrade the installed NimbusOS packages and install any new
dependencies they bring. Never waits for a lock: if apt, dpkg or
unattended-upgrades is busy, it exits with status 75 and the timer tries
again later.
.TP
.BR channel " " stable | beta " [" \-\-no\-check ]
Select the update channel. Beta adds the beta suite of the NimbusOS
repository. Going back to stable never downgrades: installed beta versions
stay until a stable release is newer.
.TP
.BR policy " " automatic | notify | off
.B automatic
installs NimbusOS updates daily;
.B notify
only checks daily;
.B off
does neither (a manual check still works).
.TP
.BR history " [" \-\-limit " " \fIN\fR]
List past apt runs from
.IR /var/log/apt/history.log ,
newest first.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print exactly one JSON document on standard output; progress goes to
standard error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/nimbusos/update.conf
Channel and policy (CHANNEL=stable|beta, POLICY=automatic|notify|off).
.TP
.I /etc/apt/sources.list.d/nimbusos.sources
The stable channel source.
.TP
.I /etc/apt/sources.list.d/nimbusos\-beta.sources
Present while the beta channel is selected.
.TP
.I /etc/apt/preferences.d/nimbusos.pref
Pinning: the NimbusOS repository may supply only NimbusOS's own packages.
.TP
.I /var/lib/nimbusos/update\-status.json
Result of the last check.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success, 1 failure, 2 usage error (for example not root), 75 busy
(another update, apt or unattended-upgrades run holds a lock).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt\-get (8),
.BR unattended\-upgrades (8),
.BR apt_preferences (5)
